A||||3||Greg Piet||I towed!||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||05-18-2000||01:19 AM||||My friends 93 Mercury sable with 60k miles lost a lifter all of a sudden, then a valve moments later.   Unfortunately it was 30 miles out of town.  So I got the call for help and brought out my 85 SE 4 speed with the newly installed class 1 tow bar.<P>I actually towed the sable home in my little Fiero!  It has turned into the chuckle of the week here we work.  "That little car towed a Mercury Sable!?!?!?!?!?" ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||05-18-2000||03:24 AM||||right on, dude!  There was one guy on here that towed his van with his Fiero!  The little car that could!||||reg||14
Z||000002||007DOUG||05-19-2000||02:03 AM||||When I bought my 84 T-top, I used my 86 V6 automatic SE to tow it home. <P>Home was 225 miles away.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/fierotow.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fierowarehouse/fierotow.jpg</A> <P>My SE is lowered 2" and has 153K. It pulled beautifully. The PA turnpike has two monster hills to climb. The SE pulled those hills at a steady 60mph with no tranny kickdowns. The temp gauge rose about 2 notches. I used a 160 thermostat.<P> On flat ground, it would do 80mph with no problem (maybe even faster, but thats stupid)<P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-19-2000||10:31 AM||||Doug--Been across the PA Pike too many times to count.  60mph across the 2 big 'uns???  Wow!!  I am impressed!  I need a 2.8.  Wait!  I have a 2.8!  YeeHaw!!||||reg||1
